40 columns                              |
>>> (trailing_commas=preserve) Kept break, call fits: siblings stay together.
foo(a,
    b, c);
<<<
foo(
  a,
  b, c
);
>>> (trailing_commas=preserve) Kept break, call overflows: everything chops.
foo(firstArgument,
    secondArgument, thirdArgumentEvenLonger);
<<<
foo(
  firstArgument,
  secondArgument,
  thirdArgumentEvenLonger
);
>>> (wrap.arguments=never) never removes developer breaks.
foo(a,
    b, c);
<<<
foo(a, b, c);
>>> Under the dart preset a kept break adds a comma; siblings stay together.
foo(a,
    b, c);
<<<
foo(
  a,
  b, c,
);
>>> (wrap.keep_existing_line_breaks=false) Flag off: breaks are not kept.
foo(a,
    b, c);
<<<
foo(a, b, c);
>>> (wrap.keep_existing_line_breaks=false) Statements stay on separate lines.
a();
b();
<<<
a();
b();
>>> Kept break between binary operands.
x = a +
    b + c;
<<<
x =
    a +
    b + c;
>>> add_when_wrapped adds a comma to a broken list.
var list = [firstElement, secondElement, third];
<<<
var list = [
  firstElement,
  secondElement,
  third,
];
>>> (wrap.chop_on_trailing_comma=false) add_when_wrapped removes it from a flat list.
foo(a, b,);
<<<
foo(a, b);
>>> (trailing_commas=remove) remove on a broken list.
function(firstArgument, secondArgument, third);
<<<
function(
  firstArgument,
  secondArgument,
  third
);
>>> (trailing_commas=remove) A required record comma is kept.
final r = (42,);
<<<
final r = (42,);
>>> Source trailing comma chops (Flutter idiom).
foo(a, b,);
<<<
foo(
  a,
  b,
);
>>> (trailing_commas=remove) The comma chops and is then removed.
foo(a, b,);
<<<
foo(
  a,
  b
);
>>> Mixed layout with a trailing comma: existing breaks decide, no chop.
foo(
  a, b,
  c,
);
<<<
foo(
  a, b,
  c,
);
>>> Mixed layout with a trailing comma: no chop when everything shares one line after the bracket.
foo(
  a, b, c,
);
<<<
foo(
  a, b, c,
);
>>> Fully chopped list with a trailing comma stays chopped.
foo(
  a,
  b,
);
<<<
foo(
  a,
  b,
);
>>> Line breaks inside an item do not make the list mixed.
foo(a, () {
  x();
},);
<<<
foo(
  a,
  () {
    x();
  },
);
>>> (wrap.keep_existing_line_breaks=false) Mixed layout without kept breaks re-lays out by policy.
foo(
  a, b,
  c,
);
<<<
foo(a, b, c);
>>> (trailing_commas=preserve wrap.chop_on_trailing_comma=false) preserve keeps a flat comma.
foo(a, b,);
<<<
foo(a, b,);
>>> (wrap.chop_on_named_arguments=[child,children]) Matching invocation chops; nested call stays flat.
Padding(padding: p, child: Text('hi'));
<<<
Padding(
  padding: p,
  child: Text('hi'),
);
>>> (wrap.chop_on_named_arguments=[child,children]) Nested list is not expanded.
Column(children: [Text('A'), Text('B')]);
<<<
Column(
  children: [Text('A'), Text('B')],
);
>>> (wrap.chop_on_named_arguments=[child]) Documented false positive.
process(child: value);
<<<
process(
  child: value,
);
>>> Empty list: no invocation is chopped.
Padding(padding: p, child: Text('hi'));
<<<
Padding(padding: p, child: Text('hi'));
